# Editor (`wiimaker edit`)

Before deep work, read `MEMORY/durable/editor.md`. After lasting discoveries, update that file.

eframe/egui shell over the same scene files agents edit via CLI. Launch: `cargo run -p wiimaker-editor -- <game>` (or `wiimaker edit`).

## Layout (keep Unity-shaped)

```
Hierarchy | Scene viewport (DrawList → framebuffer → egui texture) | Inspector
----------+--------------------------------------------------------+----------
Project: assets / scenes / cook / doctor status
```

- Hierarchy: list / create / rename / delete / select entities
- Inspector: Transform + known components; Add Component
- Viewport: live `render_world` blit; selection via Hierarchy in v0 (no IR picking yet)
- Project: browse `assets/`, surface doctor/cook warnings

## Mutation rule

All edits go through `wiimaker-scene` helpers (`add_entity`, `remove_entity`, `set_entity_transform`, `add_component_*`, `set_scene_clear`, load/save). Then set `dirty` and `rehydrate()` the preview `World`.

```rust
// ❌ BAD — edit World or invent parallel JSON writes
world.spawn(...);
serde_json::to_writer(...); // bypassing save_scene

// ✅ GOOD
add_entity(&mut self.scene, &name, &MutateOpts { .. })?;
self.dirty = true;
self.rehydrate();
// Save → save_scene(&self.scene_path, &self.scene)
```

## State pattern

`EditorApp` holds: `GameProject`, `Scene`, `scene_path`, `dirty`, `selected`, `World`, `TextureAtlas`, viewport `Framebuffer`. After asset cook/reload, rebuild atlas and rehydrate.

Play shells `wiimaker run` / `cargo run -p <game>` — do not fold egui into the fast play path.

## Out of scope (v0)

Visual scripting, full ECS UI, TEV materials, Wiimote IR picking, editing C/GX bootstrap.
